findings.evidence:
Spec §6 reset: « Aucune autorité émise encore active ni aucune valeur dépendante encore utilisable ne serait invalidée par la réinitialisation » and « une région encore effectivement utilisée ne peut être invalidée par reset ». §11 case 7 expects « Rejet ». MM-03.3.6: « Les dépendances sont transitives ».

Lean witness /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/fixlens/ResetLive.lean (`lake env lean` prints nothing, so every `decide` passes). Each step is `ok` from S3.init:
- enter the caller [meta 0, storage 1 (leaves 2, 3), dst 4], then the callee [5, 6];
- `IssueStep KA arR 0 [2] 5` creates block auth 5, held by the callee;
- `DeriveStep 5 2 .modify` creates access 6;
- `Write3Step 4 [6]`, then `DependStep 6 6`;
- `TransferStep KA 6 4 [6]`;
- `ExitStep`, after which `r7.A[6]? = some ⟨.modify, some 1, [2], 1, true⟩` (re-rooted onto internal 1).

Then `ResetStep KA r2.2 r7 (.ok (resetEff r7 r2.2))` holds, although all of these also hold:
- `r7.Usable 4 ∧ r7.D 4 = [6] ∧ r7.Active 6 ∧ ¬ r7.Active 5`;
- `ArenaInv r7 r2.2`, `I1b r7` and `ArenaResetContract KA r7 r2.2`.

After the reset, `available = [2, 3]`. Before the exit, `r5.ancs 6 = [5, 1]` and `ResetStep KA r2.2 r5 .reject` holds. `¬ (6 = anchor ∨ anchor ∈ r7.ancs 6)` holds, so arena_reset_rejects_live_dependents_underInv does not apply.

